1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hans Grabow's father (Jochim von Grabow zu Wuetiche und Grabow) and grandfather (Claus der Ältere von Grabow zu Grabow) were part of old German nobility.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans immigrated to Bornholm, but the dates are not certain although 'Dansk Adels Aarbog' mentions 1582 as his arrival in Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was first married to Barbara Huitfeldt with whom he had 3 children: Kjøn Jochum, Hans and Joachim (see tree).
2 CONT
2 CONT When Barbara died, he married Merete Pedersdatter Uf til Simblegaard (1555-1624), whose father was  Chief Justice (Landsdommer) Peder Hansen Uf til Simblegaard (1536-1596) on Bornholm. In the marriage records he was called Hans vo
2 CONC n Grabow til Pederstrup.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans and Merete did not have any children, as far as I know.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Grabow obviously kept property in Wuetiche, as his son Joachim was titled Joachim von Grabow zu Wuetiche.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Grabow bought Pederstrup, Lolland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In "Landsdommerpatriarkatet paa Bornholm - part 2" there is an interesting sentence:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Merete's stepson Jochum Grabow (i.e. Hans and Barbara Huitfeldt's son) sold all his estate [on Bornholm and perhaps Wuetiche?] and moved away from the island".
2 CONT
2 CONT This clearly places Joachim (Jochum - 1594-1634) in the tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kjøn Jochum is more difficult to find at the moment, but a close look at the names and the wives makes position and origin quite certain:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Joachim Grabow was married to Maren Hansdatter Steensen til Steensgaard (1592-1645). (See "Vore fälles aner" af C.M.Munthe, facsimile 1957, Børsums antikvariat); They had a daughter, Barbara Grabow (Jochum's mother was BARBARA 
2 CONC Huitfeldt), who got married to a Galtung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kjøn Jochum was married to (yes - you guessed it): Maren's sister Anne Hansdatter Steensen til Steensgaard (1593-1679) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) The name Jochum/Jochim/Joachim goes back to Hans von Grabow's father Jochim von Grabow zu Grabow (who died before 1594)
2 CONT
2 CONT Naming after parents and grandparents and intermarriage was normal on that time. It helped state the lineage and secured the social position - as well as maintaining the property portfolio.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information has been found at various Googled sites, entering e.g. "Hans Grabow".
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman Lee Madsens site also gives references to Bornholm (Simblegaard) on
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www3.sympatico.ca/colin.swift/myre.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT Og dette fra http://www.myerichsen.net/p33.html#i974:
2 CONT
2 CONT Medens de fleste fremmede Adelsmænd og andre højfornemme Folk, som i Tidernes Løb indvandrede til Bornholm, kom fra Skaane, var det sjældent, at der kom nogen fra Tyskland. Dette var dog Tilfældet med Hans Grabou, som blev gift me
2 CONC d Landsdommer Peder Hansens Datter, Merete Pedersdatter, paa Simblegård, og ved hende kom til at eje Simblegård fra 1609 til 1626. Han havde først været gift med Jomfru Barbara Hvitfeldt til Engstoft og havde været Befalingsmand i
2 CONC  Christianopel i 8 Aar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Medens han boede paa Simblegård, brugtes han af Kongen til adskillige Tillidshverv.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Grabow blev født cirka 1549 i Wutike, Brandenburg, Tyskland.2 Han var søn af Joachim Grabow og Else von Bretsken. Hans blev gift i 1606 i Bornholm med Margrethe Pedersdatter, datter af Peder Hansen Uf og Mette Hansdatter. Han
2 CONC s Grabow døde i 1626 i Pg. Simblegård, Klemensker, Nørre, Bornholm.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kildehenvisninger
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S283] Johan Andreas Jørgensen, Væbnere, Adel og Frimænd.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S60] Sigvard Mahler Dam, "De bornholmske væbnerslægter Uf og Splid."
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.[S41] Kristian Kure, Kures Gårdfortegnelser.
