1 OCCU Lågfrälse fogde på slottet Tre Kronor, domare, Väpnare, fogde på slottet Tre Kronor, Häradshövding i Frötuna skeppslag, Fogde och svenskt riksråd på Slottet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nils_Kettilsson_(Vasa)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Nils Kettilsson (Vasa)=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Son of Kettil 
2 CONT * King Albrecht's adviser and official at Stockholm Castle in 1354 and 1355.
2 CONT * The oldest well-educated member of the family is Nils Kettilsson (Vaasa) (died earliest 1378) who is mentioned for the first time in 1355 . [ 16 ] and first as an adult mentioned as a gunsmith , bailiff at the castle Tre Kronor 
2 CONC during the 1350s, and 1367 district chief in Frötuna shipyard in Roslagen.
2 CONT * During the revolt against Magnus Eriksson , which led to Albrekt of Mecklenburg becoming king of Sweden, Nils Kettilsson supported the Mecklenburg duke Albrekt, at least since his troops won in Sweden, and he married Christina J
2 CONC onsdotter (Rickebyätten) ( Kristiern from Ölands ) no later than 1369 grandson's daughter) which gave him entry into the Swedish nobility. Nils Kettilsson used a coat of arms similar to the Scherembekes family.
2 CONT * Nils Kettilsson had the daughters Ramborg, married to Tord Bonde , and Ingeborg, a nun in Sankta Klara kloster and possibly identical with an abbess there, and their son Kristiern. [ 17 ]
2 CONT * [http://runeberg.org/nfck/0401.html '''The Vase, Swedish genealogy, finally royal dynasty in Sweden and Poland.''']  Already in the 13th century there were three special lineages in the Roslagen with the shield mark, which from 
2 CONC Gustaf I's time due to a gradually changed form was called "the vase". The fact that they were interrelated and constituted branches of the same tribe is for many reasons very likely. Two of them were extinct already during the Mi
2 CONC ddle Ages, without actually having succeeded in raising themselves out of the provincial low nobility class. The third, on the other hand, seems to  have belonged to lower salvation at first , but it was counted from the last half
2 CONC  of the 15th century to the country's foremost high-ranking families. Its first, historically certified member was the gunner Nils Kettilsson, who is mentioned in 1361-78 (see V. 1). A son to him was the Grand Master Kristiern Nil
2 CONC sson (see V. 2), among whose sons and grandsons several took up a marked political position during the Middle Ages (see V. 3-9).  -
2 CONT * [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasa,_Skepptuna '''The name Vasa for the royal branch of this family, has origin in the Estate Wasa, known and documented under this name since it was owned by Nils Kettilsson.''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000000735972498&photo_id=6000000176449594887&position=0 '''Vasa’s Family Coat of Arms''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Vasa#TAB_8 Royal Family of Vaasa]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Kettilsson to Björnö , † after 1378. Lordship in Frötuna. (black straw vase in yellow field). King bailiff and official at Stockholm Castle in 1354 and 1355. In 1371 and 1376 he was called King Albrecht's adviser in Sweden. '
2 CONC ''Married before 1369 with Cristina Jonsdotter,''' † after 1378. Daughter of the knight Jon Nilsson Rickebyätten (seven-edged white star in blue and red field) and Märta Båth who was the daughter of Sune Joensson to Flishult .
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ramborg Nilsdotter,''' married before 1376 with the knight and the national council Tord Röriksson Bonde , † 1417-03-21 and buried in Vadstena monastery. Grandmother to King Karl Knutsson Farmer .
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Nilsdotter,''' Nun in St. Klara Kloster / A.
2 CONT * '''Christiern Nilsson,''' born 1365, died 1442-04-29 at Viborg Castle and was buried so. June 29 in Stockholm's gray brothers convent. Chief white man at Viborg. Knights, national council and drots. Married 1st with Margareta Jo
2 CONC hansdotter , † in Uppsala and buried 1413-08-07 in Vadstena monastery. Daughter of the knight Johan Moltke and Katarina Glysingsdotter . Married 2nd: 1426 to Margareta Eriksdotter born 1390, † 1451-06-09 and was buried in Gråbrödr
2 CONC aklostret in Stockholm, in her 2nd marriage . Her 1st marriage to Ture Stensson Bielke . Daughter of the Danish National Council Erik Krummedigeand Beata von Thienen 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''  Vasa Nobility 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=+10865&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermedelt
2 CONC idaAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_10865&tab=post#tab 10865]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 September 10, of issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses,  Nils Kettilsson and Kristina Jonsdotter donate with their daughter Ingeborg, which was filed in St. Klara monastery in Stockholm, 1 land in Forsa in Tensta parish to the monastery.  The issuers, together with Archbishop 
2 CONC Birger (Gregersson) in Uppsala, seal the knight Karl (Ulfsson), the lord Bo Jonsson and Tord (Röriksson) Bonde, the son-in-law of the issuers.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=10888&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermedelti
2 CONC daAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_10888&tab=post#tab 10888]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1376 October 9, of issue: Nykoping'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Issuer: Spouses,  Nils Kettilsson and Kristina Jonsdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Kettilsson, together with his wife Kristin Jonsdotter, transfers to his brother Tord Bonde and his wife Ramborg, the daughters of the issuers, and both of them heirs 13 öresland land in Norsa in Norrsunda parish, 13 öresland 
2 CONC land in Skalmsta in Skånela parish, 12 Öresland land in Norr Vidbo parish, 9 öesland land in Bergby in the same parish and 4 1/2 herb land in Rävsta in St. Olof's parish (later in Odensala parish) in Sigtuna for 150 marks of solde
2 CONC red silver, which Tord Bonde paid in full. After this date, no heirs of the issuer shall be able to exchange or revoke these properties, or any part thereof, provided that Tord Bonde and his wife Ramborg do not repay the silver su
2 CONC m paid within six months after the goods have been blamed. Kristin Jonsdotter specifically certifies that she approves the sale because the properties are her real father. The issuers further provide district governors and county 
2 CONC officials (in the areas) where the land is authorized to give their powers to Tord Bonde or his agent fixed on the properties in accordance with national law.  The guards seal together with the knight Karl Ulfsson of Tofta and Bo 
2 CONC Jonsson, throughout Sweden. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000000735972498&photo_id=6000000139799432837&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuers seal with the knight [https://www.geni.com/people/Karl-Ulfsson-Sparre-av-Tofta/6000000000346040605 Karl Ulfsson av Tofta] and  [https://www.geni.com/people/Bo-Grip/6000000003340396483 Bo Jonsson], in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=11301&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermedelti
2 CONC daAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_11301&tab=post#tab 11301]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1378 September 8, of issue: Raasepori'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bondeacknowledges in an open letter that he received from Nils Kettilsson and his wife Kristina Jonsdotter 13 Öresland land in Norsa in Norrsunda parish, 13 Öresland land in Skalmsta in Skånela parish, 12 Öresland land in Nor
2 CONC rby in Vidbo parish, 9 Öresland land in Bergby in the same parish and 4 ½ herb land in Räfsta in St. Olofs parish in Sigtuna as compensation for a debt of 150 marks of soldered silver. The properties have been leased in accordance
2 CONC  with the national law, and Tord has the spouses' open letter (DS no. 9337) thereon. He now hands over the property to his wife Ramborg. For the event Ramborg childless survives her husband, these properties must be hers. If, on t
2 CONC he other hand, she dies childless before her husband, they return, without the possibility of repurchase, to Nils Kettilsson and his wife Kristina, for the great love and goodwill that they have shown the issuer and which he still
2 CONC  hopes for. The issuer seals together with the knight Erengisle Nilsson. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000000735972498?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000139804244821
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals together with the knight [https://www.geni.com/people/Erengisle-Nilsson-Hammersta/6000000003734498678 Erengisle Nilsson]. (Married with Kristina Röriksdotter Bonde sister to Tord Röriksson Bonde)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sdhk?EndastDigitaliserat=false&SDHK=11322&TrycktUtgava=true&TrycktRegest=true&Brevtext=true&Extratext=true&Sigill=true&Original=true&MedeltidaAvskrifter=true&MedeltidaRegest=true&Eftermedelti
2 CONC daAvskrifter=true&EftermedeltidaRegest=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_11322&tab=post#tab 11322]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1378 October 24, Issuer: Nils Kettilsson (Vaasa) and his wife Kristin Jonsdotter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Kettilsson and Kristina Jonsdotter give their servant Olof Lammfot 12 öresland land with, among other things, mills and mill streams in Vallby in the Rimbo parish in Seven Hundred with full ownership. If Olof dies childless, 
2 CONC the property returns to Nils and Kristin's heirs, but if Olof has children, the property becomes their inheritance. The issuers authorize the district governor and the county clerk in the same hardened authority to give to Olof or
2 CONC  his representative the property under the national law.  The issuers seal together with Nils Petersson in Länna. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000000735972498?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000139810055821
2 CONT
