2 CONT * About Raseborg's Chr. Lovén, Castles and fortifications in medieval Sweden (1996), pp. 156-160.
2 CONT * For the letter's tradition via Cecilia Stenbock's archive at Haga see L. Sjödin in MRA 1943, p. 58.
2 CONT * Compare Nils Kettilsson's letter 1376 9/10 (DS no. 9337) in which these current properties are sold to Tord Bonde., See SDHK No. 10888
2 CONT * Äldre svenska frälsesläkter, vol II:1 s 103-4.
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcriptions:  BE Hd III
2 CONT * Post-medieval regest / note:  Listed in Three Roses estate archives 1561
2 CONT * DS 9825, HSH 36, supra. p. 7, Västergötlands Fornminnesförening magazine II: 8-9, p. 150 (of U 303 a, fol. B 11, KB).
2 CONT * Three Roses Goods Archive 1561, printed in Västergötland's Fornminnesförening magazine II: 8-9 (1908), p. 150.
2 CONT * About Nils Kettilsson (Vaasa) and his wife Kristina Jonsdotter (Rickebyätten) see H. Gillingstam, Ätterna Oxenstierna and Vasa, p. 158 ff. (this letter p. 169, note 280).
2 CONT * About Olof Lammfot, who was still alive at the beginning of the 1400s when he sold several farms to Tord Röriksson Bonde, see Västergötlands Fornminnesförening magazine II: 8-9 (1908), pp. 152 and 170.
2 CONT * For Vallby see DMS, Uppland 1: 5, p. 149.
2 CONT * About the county clerk's office (in Uppland) see KL X: Lensmann, sp. 509 et seq., Especially sp. 511-512.
2 CONT *Genom sekler: bilder ur en svensk storätts lif, by Anders Ramsay - https://books.google.com/books?id=cVE_AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA270&lpg=PA270&dq=Nils+Kettilsson+(Vasa),+to+Bj%C3%B6rn%C3%B6&source=bl&ots=So_Sqh9300&sig=ACfU3U3zhucfkBrmCC-v
