1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DO NOT CONFUSE WITH BIRGITTA TORDSDOTTER. Tordsdotter is often confused as Erik Johansson’s mother, but is actually just Anne’s. ==Birgitta Gustavsdotter (Sture)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Gustaf Anundsson Sture (Sjöblad) and Birgitta Stensdotter (Bielke) 
2 CONT *Birth:  1440-04-01 in Rydboholm, Östra Ryd (AB) 
2 CONT * Death: September 05, 1472 (30) in Rydboholm, Östra Ryd, Uppland, Sweden(barnsäng)  
2 CONT * Place of Burial: in Östra Ryds kyrka, Uppland, Sweden 
2 CONT * Rydboholm was Birgitta Gustavsdotter's heirloom.
2 CONT * She belonged to the Sea Leaf branch of Stureätten, (Source: Lars-Olof Larsson - Gustav Vasa - national father or tyrant)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  '''Johan Kristiernsson (Vasa),''' (c. 1426– 4 June 1477 at Rydboholms Castle, Östra Ryd) was a Swedish statesman and Knight, son of Krister Nilsson ( The Royal) and Margareta Eriksdotter Krummedige.  Johan Kristiernsso
2 CONC n was enrolled at the University of Leipzig 1444, but was dubbed a knight only a few years later.  Savior/Surname: The Vasa dynasty, Seat yard:  Rydboholms Castle, Father, Parents:  Nilsson (Vasa) & Margareta Eriksdotter Krummedig
2 CONC e
2 CONT
2 CONT * Johan Kristiernsson (Vasa), Titles, Knight, District Judge in Vallentuna County, Swedish statesman, Period, 3 July 1457, Appointed by The Union King Kristian I
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christiern Johansson,''' Cristiern Johansson Vaasa to Örby, Vendel / C, † about 1494–97. The Swedish National Council and the Chief Magistrate at Kalmar Castle. Married to Dorotea Knutsdotter in her 1st marriage (her 2nd marr
2 CONC iage about 1511 to Gunnar Larsson to Hornby ). Daughter of the knight and national council Knut Eskilsson Banér and Kristina Eriksdotter Örnfot .
2 CONT * '''Erik Johansson,''' executed at Stockholm massacre 1520-11-08. Chief of Danderyd and Rydbo ship team. Knights and national council. He was, as a person, rather insidious, arrogant, conflict-prone, hot-tempered and, in addition
2 CONC , very violent. Pleaded before the court several times for committing crimes. One of the crimes was theft in Ekerö church building, another was the murder of a man who illegally invaded Erik's yard. '''Married about 1492-95 with C
2 CONC ecilia Magnusdotter,''' daughter of the Swedish National Council Magnus Karlsson (Ekaätten) and Sigrid Eskilsdotter Banér . The widow Cecilia and her daughters died in Danish captivity in 1522.
2 CONT * '''Katarina Johansdotter,'' twin,''' born and † 1472.
2 CONT * '''Margareta Johansdotter twin,''' born and † 1472.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Adelsvapen-Wiki Family of Birgitta Gustavsdotter (Sture)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: Gustav Sture (son of Anund Sture, tab. 5). Mentioned no earlier than 1438. Occurs as national council from the same year. Was knight between 8.7 1441 and 5.1 1442, ie at King Kristof's coronation 14.9 1441. Was captain a
2 CONC t Älvsborg 7.9 1441. Was 3.4 1443 and at his dead chieftain in Kalmar. Lived even 2.1 1444 but was dead 29.1 s .. Dismissed probably 26.1 1444. Married before 29.8 1438 with Birgitta Stensdotter , daughter of the national council 
2 CONC Sten Turesson ( Bielke ) and Margareta Karlsdotter ( Sparre of Tofta ). Before 12 February 1447 Mrs Birgitta was re-enacted with the knight and later the National Council and the lawyer in Uppland Gustav Karlsson ( Gumsehuvud ).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Anund Sture'''. Mentioned at the earliest on 2.1 1461 and was then already a knight. Died 12.6 1463 at Riddarholmen in Stockholm, buried in Toresund's church in Selebo hd in Södermanland and written on the gravestone to Rävsn
2 CONC äs in the aforementioned sn.
2 CONT * '''Birgitta Gustavsdotter'''  Named the unmarried 1453. Died 1472. Was married to the National Council and knight Johan Kristiernsson (Vaasa) before 2.1.161, who by 1474 was re-married with Birgitta Tordsdotter in her former mar
2 CONC ried, daughter of the marshal Tord Bonde and Iliana Åkesdotter ( Tott ).
2 CONT * '''Sten Sture''', now called "Sten Sture the Elder". In 1477 is stated to be 30 years old, which would mean that he then did not turn 40 years, ie was born at the earliest 1437. First mentioned in 2.1 1461 and was already then k
2 CONC night. Was the chieftain of Västergötland in the summer of 1469. At the time of Karl Knutsson's death, 15.5, 1470, was the chief of the Stockholm, Örebro and Turku castles and called himself 1.6 1470 "the ruler of the state up thi
2 CONC s time". Acclaimed as the National Director in Arboga about 1.5 1471 Recognized 6.10 1497 King Hans and received 3.12 1497 of this entire Turku diocese, Nyköping County with Näveberg, Rekarne, Färingön, Sorunda and Ösmo snr at Söd
2 CONC ertörn and Götala wasteland in Västergötland as sermon. Was under the King His Government Chief of Law. Made in the summer of 1501 rebellion against this and was elected 12.11 in 1501 again to the national governor. Died 14.12 150
2 CONC 3 in Jönköping.Tott ) and Märta Bengtsdotter ( Vinstorpaätten ). Mrs. Ingeborg died at the end of 1507. Before the marriage with Sten Sture she had 11.3 in 1464 been betrothed with the not long after the death of Hans Sigurdssönn 
2 CONC ( Yngre Sudreimsätten ), of which she received a morning gift in Kållands hd in Västergötland. By King Hans, she received a lifetime right in the county of Hämeenlinna. In addition, as a widow, Satakunda was a county but abstained
2 CONC  from Sten Sture's other counties in 1504. Sten Sture d., Except marriage had a daughter Birgitta, who became nun in Vadstena monastery 9.10 1485 and died 27.6 1536
2 CONT
