1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married three times:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester (before 1655) Hannah (circa 1666) Elizabeth  Thomas(circa 1670)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a farmer. He was a Quaker minister. He resided circa 1651 at West River, Anne Arundel Co., MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cole II was born in 1633 in the Puritan area near Jamestown, VA to William and Sarah Cole. He grew up there, then moved with his father to St. Mary's Co., MD in 1650. In 1655 he married Hester ____ at Severn, MD and was es
2 CONC tablished in Severn by 1656. His first child, William Cole III was born on 9/26/1655. In 1657 two influential visitors, Thomas Thurston and Josiah Coale came and preached to a growing group of Friends (Quakers). William started wr
2 CONC iting his name Coale after this. At this time William II associated with older relative, Thomas Cole. In 1658 William refused to bear arms in the militia and was subjected to land penalties. In 1660 William moved his family to the
2 CONC  West River in AnnArundal Co., MD. West River is 30 miles south of Baltimore on the western shore of Chesapeake Bay. He owned 150 acres called "Great Bonnerston". Hester evidently died because in 1666 he married Hannah Galloway, t
2 CONC he widow of Richard Galloway, in Ann Arundal Co., MD. They had a son, William Cole, IV born on 10/20/1667 at West River, Ann Arundal Co., MD. Jack Cole of Huntsville, AL believes they also had a son John born in 1669. Hannah proba
2 CONC bly died in childbirth because her dateof death is November, 1669. In 1670 he married a third time to Elizabeth Thomas, daughter of Philip and Sarah Harrison Thomas. William II bought 500 acres on the Patuxent River called "Portla
2 CONC nd Manor" and another 100 acre tract called "Hickory Hills". In 1672 a dynamic English Founder of Society of Friends visited William. In 1676 William II moved from "Great Bonnerston" to "Portland Manor". William III took over the 
2 CONC old homestead "Great Bonnerston" and William IV took over "Hickory Hills". William II died in 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://edlers.org/pers/AP/06bcole.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William3 Coale, born about 1632 in VA, accompanied his father to St Jerome, St Mary's Co MD. LaterWilliam went on to Anne Arundel Co MD. He married Hester [Cole] about 1654; at least one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT He adopted Quakerism, probably before 1657, about the same time as his uncle Thomas Cole, page 6b-3. William changed the spelling of his name from Cole to Coale, probably in admiration of Josiah Coale, a famous Quaker missionary (
2 CONC no known relation). By 1662 William was minister of the West River Meeting of the Society of Friends of Anne Arundel Co MD. He and George Wilson traveled in VA, probably during the early 1660s, as “Messengers of the Truth”. This w
2 CONC asn't popular there, and they were imprisoned for many months. George died “in irons” and, although William survived, his health was permanently impaired.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hannah [Coale] about 1666; at least one child. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Thomas about 1670; at least three children. Her parents were Philip Thomas and Sarah Harrison.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Elizabeth lived comfortably on the West River, Anne Arundel Co, the rest of their lives.24 He died 30 Oct 1678 Great Bonnerton Plantation, near West River, age about 46. She died before 24 Feb 1726, when her will was p
2 CONC roved.
2 CONT
