2 TITL Biographical Summaries of Notable People
1 NOTE "OF DENMARK"
1 NOTE born Dec. 12, 1574 died March 2, 1619
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT Queen consort of James I (1566-1625) of Great Britain (James VI of Scotland); although she had little direct political influence, her extravagant expenditures contributed to the financial difficulties that plagued James's regime.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT The daughter of King Frederick II of Denmark and Norway, Anne was married to James in 1589. Her Lutheran upbringing and frivolous nature cost her the affection of James's Scottish Presbyterian subjects, and James alienated Anne by
2 CONC  entrusting the upbringing of their first son, Prince Henry (1594ΓÇô1612), to John Erskine, 2nd earl of Mar. Nevertheless, after James ascended the British throne in 1603, he and Anne lived in harmony, although they had separate q
2 CONC uarters during the last few years of her life. Most of the Queen's time and energy were devoted to lavish court entertainments, and her patronage contributed to the development of the arts, particularly of the masque. She embarras
2 CONC sed James, however, by displaying sympathy for Roman Catholicism. Their second son succeeded James as King Charles I (ruled 1625ΓÇô49).
1 NOTE Anne of Denmark, 1574-1619, queen consort of James I of England, daughter of Frederick II of Denmark and Norway. She married James in 1589 and was crowned with him at Windsor in 1603. Court entertainments and the embellishment of 
2 CONC buildings interested her more than affairs of state. Although not openly a Catholic, Anne attended Mass privately and refused communion in the Church of England. Of her six children, the three who survived infancy were Henry, prin
2 CONC ce of Wales (d. 1612); Charles (later Charles I); and Elizabeth (later electress palatine and queen of Bohemia). [The Illustrated Columbia Encyclopedia, 1969]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of Denmark (1574-1619), daughter of Frederick II born to Skanderborg. In 1589 she was married to James VI of Scotland. She was crowned with him in Westminster in 1603. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
2 CONT
2 CONT The daughter of Frederick II, King of Denmark. [GADD.GED]
2 CONT
2 CONT Also have birth as 12 Dec 1574.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also have death as 2 Mar 1619.
