3 TEXT Anne of Denmark has not been well treated by historians. For instance, Maurice Lee commented in 1959 that ‘she was not an interesting woman. She had no particular distinction of mind or spirit. She showed occasional neurotic tende
4 CONC ncies, she enjoyed intrigue, she was stupid, and she bore grudges’ (Lee, 204).
