2 CONT ==[http://samla.raa.se/xmlui/bitstream/handle/raa/1098/1935_237.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y SIGGE GUTTORMSSON TO LJUM AND HIS GRAVSTONE 1 ALVASTRA RECONSTRUCTION OF A 1200TH GRAPH OF SOLVE GARDELL]
2 CONT
2 CONT + r (I0: IIXVSQK6 enom; PARIdö; aöivxH5 .Amoiu + si6Go; ouisGinA; aonövn © vRQ.i .. siavnA: • K..AI XI ... SVS
2 CONT GenviGOVKPKe6eneRosvs + nomme-BjRGeKvs-GovQs: nvno nuoctor 010.1PR006RUS
2 CONT
2 CONT With the help of both images, Brenners and Abildgaards, I will seek to reconstruct the burial text below. First of all, it is apparent from the content that the stone was originally made over a true couple, Sigge and Christina. Th
2 CONC ese can be easily identified as Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna and his wife Christina, daughter of Birger Jarl in his first married to Ingeborg, Erik Läspes sister. About the two spouses, Sigge died in 1283 and Christina 1285. The dat
2 CONC e of the grave stone is thus given.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition, the inscription is written on leonine hexameter, which, to some extent, facilitates reconstruction. The text consists of four verses. The first difficulty encountered in the text presented is the term coniunxit in the
2 CONC  first verse, which undoubtedly seems to be misunderstood, since this reading is linguistically impossible in this context. Both sources, however, have the same readings, and therefore it must be considered unlikely that both reco
2 CONC rders would have made the same mistakes in the recording of the grave text. Thus, it appears that the neighbor's expression has really been impregnated with the gravestone in question. The only explanation for the text site must b
2 CONC e that the stonecutter here made a mistake by reversing two letters, ie v. S. Concealed an IV instead of the correct VI of the original manuscript. Reading convixit seems
2 CONT
2 CONT I am the only acceptable one to this place. About the term
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 convivers also have the Thesaurus remark 'frequens in ti- tulis sepulcralibus de conjugibus ", and in our text the inscription is true spouses. The object of verb form is apparently amori. As for this case, Thesaurus suggests, a
2 CONC s an example, dative expression. put Christo convivimus, and with Diehl in his register to Inscript. Christ. veter. p. 338 are several references to the design vivere deo. However, Armini has shown in Eranos that wiveling also rul
2 CONC es ablative - the amorphism of the text could consequently
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 is cleared as a vulgarlatic form for the pure classic amore. To It is precisely this form that occurs in this handled grave text, I think it is most likely, although I would like to admit that the change of meaning between the t
2 CONC wo casualties between at least our texts does not matter. For it can be quite indifferent in this place, if you reproduce the translation with the phrase "lived in love" or "lived together for love." In classical latitude, the ter
2 CONC m "in amore vivere" is known as the term "familiar".
2 CONT
2 CONT Even the second verse must be conjunciated. The rhyme word is here Christina. The last word of the bar must therefore have a similar ending letter. Both of our texts, Brenners and Abildgaards, correspond so far that they both end 
2 CONC on '-syna'. The former, however, precedes the latter word 'OS: PE', the latter on the other hand '. . . . E ». Brenner's "OS" is, of course, a misrepresentation of the simplicity -que, whose true epigraphic representation, bl. a. 
2 CONC is evident from Abildgaardstexten's "Gutthormque". Thus remains to explain the gap after -que. For metric reasons, a dactylose must be followed, whose last syllable ends with an E, when both texts have the same vocabulary. Under s
2 CONC uch circumstances, only two possibilities seem to me to be given, namely either the writing 'ELE: SYNA' or 'ELEE: SYNA', ie both of these writing should be perceived as an epigraphic expression of the medium-term line 'elemo eyes'
2 CONC  or 'eleeraosyna'. Both forms are present, but of course the first one should be preferred for the meter. The middle of the list should be that the stone has been produced by means of abbreviation characters in an analogy with, fo
2 CONC r example, the letter hore = honore. Second worsened should be read as follows: Siggo Cristina / Condimturque Elemosyna.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOLVE GARDELL: Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna and his grave Stone in Alvastra.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Kgl. The Stockholm library has a 17th century manuscript with illustrations of medieval tombstones, many of which have now disappeared. One of them once covered the grave of a married couple in the monastery church of Alvastra
2 CONC , which in the second half of the thirteenth century belonged to the noblest magnate-families of the country. The Medieval Latin epitaph, which is written in impeccable Leoninian hexameters, attempts to reconstruct the author part
2 CONC ly with the help of a later reproduction of the stone from the middle of the 18th century, partly with conjectures according to the classical philological method. The inscription should be of greater interest to Swedish cultural h
2 CONC istory, as the couple, Sigge to Ljuna and Christina, Birger Jarl's daughter, are previously known through several documents, which are appended to the text by the author.
2 CONT
2 CONT See complete research in Swedish listed below 
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://samla.raa.se/xmlui/bitstream/handle/raa/1098/1935_237.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y Journal of Swedish Antiquarian Research]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#Chapter3 Project MedLands, Sweden Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chapter 3.  KINGS of SWEDEN 1250-1412 (FOLKINGAÄTTEN)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIRGER Magnusson, son of MAGNUS "Minnesköld" [Folkungaätten] & his second wife Ingrid [Ylva] '''([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Sv
2 CONC ecia" in 1248[173].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founder of Stockholm.  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj
2 CONC  ac Benedictj Scolaris”[174].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1265 of "Birgerus dux Sveciæ"[175]. 
2 CONT '''married firstly ([1235]) INGEBORG of Sweden, daughter of ERIK Knutsson King of Sweden & his second wife Richeza of Denmark''' ([1212]-17 Jun 1254).  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 4 Nov 1246 in which “Ericus…rex S
2 CONC wethie” names “domino Birgero genero nostro”[176].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  '''married secondly (1261) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Holstein, widow of ABEL King of Denmark, d
2 CONC aughter of ADOLF IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe''' (1225-1288, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Annales Stadenses record the marriage "1237 VII Kal Mai" of "dux Abel" and "filiam comitis Adolfi de Scowenborc
2 CONC h", naming her "Mechtildem" and recording her second marriage to "ducem Sueciæ" in a later passage[177].  The Icelandic Annals record the marriage in 1261 of "Bergerus Sveciæ dux" and "Mathildam reginam Daniæ"[178].  Mistress (1):
2 CONC  ---.  The name of Birger's mistress is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson & his first wife INGEBORG of Sweden had eight children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.     '''    RIKISSA Birgersdotter''' (-before 13 Dec 1288).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Rixam filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Henricum seniorem [filium Nycolai domini de Werle]"[179].  The primary source which confi
2 CONC rms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  '''married firstly (Oslo 1251) HAAKON Haakonsson,''' "den Unge/the Young" under King of Norway, son of HAAKON IV "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wife Margareta Skulesdo
2 CONC tter (Bergen 10 Nov 1232-Tønsberg 30 Apr or 5 May1257, bur Oslo, St Hallvards Church).  m secondly (1262) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Werle, son of NIKOLAUS I Herr von Werle zu Rostock [Mecklenburg] & his wife Jutta von Anhalt
2 CONC  (-murdered near Saal, Rügen 8 Oct 1291).  Herr zu Werle zu Güstrow 1281. 
2 CONT * 2.        ''' VALDEMAR Birgersson''' ([1237]-Nyköping Castle 26 Dec 1302).  The Icelandic Annals record that "Valdemarus Birgiri filius" succeeded as king of Sweden in 1249[180].  He succeeded in 1250 as VALDEMAR King of Sweden.
2 CONC   “Waldemarus…rex Swechie” confirmed the donation of property to Gudhems Kloster by “reginam dominam Katerinam” by charter dated 17 Jan 1251 which names “patris nostri domini Byrgerj ducis”[181].  The Annales Lubicenses records th
2 CONC at "Waldemarus rex Sweorum" was deposed in 1275 by "Magno duce fratre suo"[182].  The Icelandic Annals record the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus" and the departure of Valdemar for Denmark soon after[183].  The I
2 CONC celandic Annals record the death in 1302 of "Valdemarus Birgeri filius Rex Sveonum"[184].  '''married firstly (1260, divorced after 1276) SOPHIE of Denmark,''' daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of 
2 CONC Saxony (-1286).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[185].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence 
2 CONC of "Sophia regina Valdimari regis, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[186].  '''
2 CONC married secondly LUCARDIS,''' daughter of ---.  1296.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.   '''Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark,''' daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wif
2 CONC e Jutta of Saxony ([1246]-[1286/95]).  Abbess of St Agneta in Roskilde 1266.  She left the convent in 1271[187]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' King Valdemar & his first wife SOPHIE of Denmark had seven children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)        ''' ERIK Valdemarsson''' (-1261, bur Sigruna Abbey).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>* b)         '''INGEBORG Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1290]).  The Annales Lubicenses refer to the first wife of "Gherardi comitis Holtzatiæ" as "filia Woldemari Regis Sweciæ"[188].  “Waldemarus…Rex Sveorum” confirmed a grant to Hamb
2 CONC urg by “pater noster Dominus Byrgerus felicis memoriæ Dux Sveorum” by charter dated 12 Dec 1275 “in nuptiis filiæ nostræ…et comitis Gerardi…de Holsatia”[189].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia regina Valdimari reg
2 CONC is, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[190].  m (12 Dec 1275) as his first wife,
2 CONC  GERHARD II Graf von Holstein in Plön, son of GERHARD I Graf von Holstein in Itzehoe & his first wife Elisabeth von Mecklenburg (1254-Plön 28 Oct 1312, bur Hamburg Cathedral).
2 CONT >>>>* c)         '''KATARINA Valdemarsdotter''' (-1283).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[191].
2 CONC
2 CONT >>>>* d)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' [Folkungaättens Valdemarsgren] ([1271/72]-1330).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico 
2 CONC annos quinque nato" in 1276[192].  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[193].  The Icelandic Annals 
2 CONC record that "domicellus Ericus filius Valdemari" was released from prison in 1302[194].  Norwegian High Councillor 1308.  Swedish High Councillor 1322.  m INGEBORG Knutsdotter, daughter of KNUT Jonsson [Aspenäsätten] & his wife Ka
2 CONC tharina Bengtsdotter [Folkungaättens lagmansgren].  1333.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>* i)         ''' VALDEMAR Eriksson'''  1345/69.  m firstly (before 1347) INGEGÄRD Karlsdotter [Färla], daughter of [KARL Orestason [Färla] & his wife Helena Magnusdotter [Folkungaättens oäkta gren]].  m secondly as her firs
2 CONC t husband, HELGA Anundsdotter [Balk av Strand], daughter of ANUND Röriksson [Balk av Strand] & his wife Cecilia Magnusdotter.  She married secondly (before 1379) Ya Königsmarck, Vogt of Stockholm Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Valdemar & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>(a)       ERIK Valdemarsson (-[1388/96]).  m ERMEGARD --- (-[1402/03].
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* e)       '''  RIKISSA Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1 Sep 1288/19 Apr 1293]).  The Annales Polonorum record the marriage "1285 in octavis sancti Francisci" of "filiam regis Swecie nomine Rithcam" and "dux Primislius maioris Polonie"
2 CONC [195].  m (1285) as his second wife, PRZEMYSŁ Prince of Greater Poland, son of PRZEMYSŁ I Prince of Poznan, Kalisch and Gniezien [Piast] & his wife Elisabeth von Schlesien [Piast] (14 Oct 1257-murdered Rogoźno 8 Feb 1296, bur Pose
2 CONC n Cathedral).  He succeeded in 1295 as PRZEMYSŁ II King of Poland. 
2 CONT >>>>* f)          '''MARIANNA Valdemarsdotter''' The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   1299.  m (Nyköping 1285) as his second wife, RUDOLF von Diepholz, son of --- (-1303 or af
2 CONC ter).
2 CONT >>>>* g)         '''MARGARETA Valdemarsdotter'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.   Nun at Skänninge Convent 1288. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Valdemar had one possible illegitimate son by Mistress (1):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* h)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' ([1273]-).  Brenner doubts his existence, saying he is likely confused with King Valdemar's legitimate son Erik[196].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3.         '''MAGNUS Ladulås Birgersson''' ([1240]-Visingsö 18 Dec 1290, bur Stockholm, Riddarholm Church).  The Annales Lubicenses names "Magno duce fratre suo [=Waldemarus rex Sweorum]" when recording that he deposed his broth
2 CONC er in 1275[197].  He succeeded in 1275 as MAGNUS I Ladulås King of Sweden.   
2 CONT * 4.         '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter (-after 1285).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   m SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna (-bur Alvastra Abbey).'''
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATARINA''' The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Katerinam, filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Sifridum comitem"[198].  m (before 17 Oct 1259) SIEGFRIED Graf von Anhalt in Köthen und Dessau, son of HEINRICH I "der Fe
2 CONC tte" Graf von Anhalt und Aschersleben & his wife Irmgard von Thüringen (-after 25 Mar 1298, bur Coswig).
2 CONT * 6.         '''ERIK Birgersson''' (-17 Dec 1275).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolaris”[199]
2 CONC .  Duke in southern Sweden 1275. 
2 CONT * 7.      '''   INGEBORG '''(-30 Jun 1302, bur Mölln).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie refers to the wife of "Iohannem [filium Alberti dux]" as "filiam regis Suecie"[200].  The Annales Lubicenses record the death in 1302 of "Ingebu
2 CONC rgis, mater Alberti, Iohannis et Erici ducum Saxoniæ, filia Regis Sweonum"[201].  m ([1270]) JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, son of ALBRECHT I Herzog zu Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen [Askanier] & his third wife Helene von Braunschwei
2 CONC g (-30 Jul 1286).
2 CONT * 8.         '''BENGT Birgersson''' ([1254]-25 May 1291).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolari
2 CONC s”[202].  Duke in Finland 1284.  Bishop of Linköping 1286. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson had one illegitimate son by Mistress (1):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9.        '''  GREGERS Birgersson or Frilloson''' [Folkingaättens oäkta gren] (-1276, bur Uppsala).  At Ängsjö.  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1276 of "Gregorius filius notus Birgeri comitis"[203].  He was ancestor of
2 CONC  the Folkingaättens Oäkta Gren family. 
