1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#Adalasiadied1285
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ALESSINA (-6 Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonefacius Montisferrati marchio", dated 12 Jun 1253, bequeathes property to "Alaxinam filiam meam inpuberem", appoints "Guilelminum filium meum inpuberem" as his heir, substit
2 CONC uting in turn "Alaxinam…filia mea" and "Tomam de Saluciis", if his son died childless[222].  The marriage contract between “duci Bruneswik” and “sororem marchionis Montis Ferati” is dated 6 Oct 1262[223].  The Annales Londonienses
2 CONC  record the marriage in 1267 of "dux de Bruneswiche" and "filiam Marchisi de Monteferato, cognatam regine" at Kenilworth[224].  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "filiam marchionis Montis-Ferrati Aleidem" as second wife of "Albe
2 CONC rtus"[225].  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "relictam Alberti ducis de Brunsvic Aleidem filiam marchionis Montis-Ferrati" as the second wife of "Gerardus"[226].  The Libro Memoriarum Sancti Blasii records the death in Feb 128
2 CONC 5 of "Allexina ducissa in Brunswich et cometissa Holsacie, soror comitis Montisferranum"[227].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (contract 6 Oct 1262, Kenilworth 1 Nov 1266) as his second wife, ALBRECHT I "der Große" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg, son of OTTO I “dem Kind” Herzog von Braunschweig & his wife Mathilde von Brandenburg [As
2 CONC kanier] (1236-Braunschweig 15 Aug 1279, bur Braunschweig Cathedral).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1282) as his second wife, GERHARD I Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg zu Itzehoe, son of ADOLF IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe (1232-21 Dec 1290).
