1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingeborg von Mecklenburg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * INGEBORG von Mecklenburg ([1340]-after 25 Jul 1395, bur Itzehoe).  
2 CONT * Daughter of Albert II duke of Mecklenburg-Schwerin and Princess Eufemia Van Zweden, of Sweden and Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  firstly (contract Pritzwalk 25 Jun 1357, Feb 1360) as his second wife, '''LUDWIG VI Duke of Bavaria Markgraf von Brandenburg''', son of Emperor LUDWIG IV King of Germany, Duke of Bavaria Pfalzgraf bei Rhein & his secon
2 CONC d wife Marguerite de Hainaut [Avesnes] Ctss de Hainaut, Holland and Zeeland (Rome 7 May 1328-Berlin 17 May 1365, bur Berlin Church of the Franciscan Order). 
2 CONT *  Married:  secondly (before 1374) as his second wife, '''HEINRICH II "der Eiserne" Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg''', son of GERHARD III "der Grosse" Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg & his wife Sophie von Werle [Mecklenburg] ([1317]-[
2 CONC 16 Oct 1384/12 Jun 1389], bur Itzehoe). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MECKLENBURG.htm#AlbrechtIIdied1379A Project MedLands Norway Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT HEINRICH von Holstein-Rendsburg ([1317]-[16 Oct 1384/12 Jun 1389], bur Itzehoe).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Hinricus ferreus et Nicolaus et Iohannes" as the sons of "Gerardi Magni comitis"[195].  He succeeded his f
2 CONC ather in 1340 as HEINRICH II "der Eiserne" Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg.  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ records the death of "Ferreus Henricus comes" in 1381 and his burial "in speulchro partum suorum in Idzeho"[196].  '''m firstly MECHT
2 CONC ILD zur Lippe,''' daughter of BERNHARD [V] Herr zur Lippe & his wife Richardis von der Mark (-[15 Jun 1362/12 Mar 1365]).  '''m secondly (before 1374) '''as her second husband, INGEBORG von Mecklenburg, widow of LUDWIG VI Duke of 
2 CONC Bavaria Markgraf von Brandenburg, daughter of ALBRECHT II "der Große" Herzog von Mecklenburg & his first wife Eufemia Eriksdatter of Sweden ([1340]-after 25 Jul 1395, bur Itzehoe).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Graf Heinrich II & his first wife MECHTILD zur Lippe had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          '''MECHTILD''' (- after 12 Mar 1365). 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Graf Heinrich II & his second wife INGEBORG von Mecklenburg had four children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * ii)         '''GERHARD von Holstein-Rendsburg'''(- killed in battle Süderhamme 5 Aug 1404, bur Itzehoe).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Gerardum primum ducem Sleszwiccensem et Albertum et Hinricum comites" as the son
2 CONC s of "comes Hinricus [ferreus]"[197].  He succeeded in 1382 as GERHARD VI Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg.  He succeeded in 1386 as Herzog von Schleswig. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''see Chapter 2.B. HERZOGEN von SCHLESWIG.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * iii)        '''ALBRECHT von Holstein-Rendsburg''' ( Dithmarschen 28 Sep 1403, bur Itzehoe).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Gerardum primum ducem Sleszwiccensem et Albertum et Hinricum comites" as the sons of "comes H
2 CONC inricus [ferreus]"[198].  He succeeded in 1384 as ALBRECHT II Graf von Holstein-Segeberg, and his uncle in 1397 as Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg.  m (before 23 Mar 1399) AGNES von Sachsen-Lauenburg, daughter of ERICH IV Herzog von S
2 CONC achsen-Lauenburg & his wife Sophie von Braunschweig (-before 1415).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ refers to, but does not name, the wife of "Albertum [fratrem Gherardi ducis Sleszwiccensis et Holtzacie]" as "de domo ducum Saxonie", spe
2 CONC cifying that they left no heirs[199]. 
2 CONT * iv)       '''HEINRICH''' (-Bordesholm Feb 1421).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Gerardum primum ducem Sleszwiccensem et Albertum et Hinricum comites" as the sons of "comes Hinricus [ferreus]", in a later passage spec
2 CONC ifying that Heinrich was elected "episcopus Osnabrugensis"[200].  Canon at Münster Cathedral 1402.  Bishop of Osnabrück 1402, resigned 1404.  He succeeded in 1404 as HEINRICH III Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg.  
2 CONT * v)        '''SOPHIE''' (-after 1451).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ refers to the daughter of "Ferreus Henricus comes" as wife of "duci Pomeraniæ"[201].  m ([1398]) BOGISLAW VIII Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern, son of BOGISLAW V 
2 CONC Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern & his second wife Adelheid von Braunschweig ([1363/68]-11 Feb 1418). 
2 CONT * b)         '''NIKOLAUS of Holstein-Rendsburg''' ([1321]-8 May 1397, bur Itzehoe).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Hinricus ferreus et Nicolaus et Iohannes" as the sons of "Gerardi Magni comitis", specifying that Nikol
2 CONC aus died without male heirs[202].  He succeeded in 1390 as NIKOLAUS Graf von Holstein-Rendsburg.  m (1354) as her second husband, ELISABETH von Braunschweig-Lüneburg, widow of OTTO von Sachsen-Wittenberg, daughter of WILHELM Joint
2 CONC  Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Lüneburg & his first wife Hedwig von Ravensberg (-17 Apr 1384).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ refers to the wife of "Nicolaus comes" as mother of "Alberti ducis Saxonie"[203].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Graf Nikolaus & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          '''ELISABETH''' (-25 Jan 1416, bur Cammin). m firstly ALBRECHT IV Herzog von Mecklenburg, son of HEINRICH III Herzog von Mecklenburg-Schwerin & his first wife Ingeborg of Denmark (-before 24 Jun [1387/88]).  m second
2 CONC ly (1404) as his first wife, ERICH V Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of ERICH IV Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife Sophie von Braunschweig (-end 1435). 
2 CONT * c)         '''ADOLF''' ([1330]-after 1359).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Hinricus ferreus et Nicolaus et Iohannes" as the sons of "Gerardi Magni comitis"[204]. 
2 CONT * d)         '''ELISABETH''' ([1340]-1402).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ refers to the daughter of "Gerardi Magni comitis" as "claustralis in Elten abbatissa, prius copulata regis Swecie et in mari prohibita"[205]. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''GISELBERT''' (-[20 Dec 1343/25 May 1344]).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names (in order) "Ghiselbertem archiepiscopum Bremensem…magnum Gherardum comitem et Iohannem fratrem eius" as the heirs of "Hinricum comitem"[206]
2 CONC .  Canon of St Gereon at Köln before 1324.  Canon at Lübeck Cathedral 1327.  Canon at Bremen Cathedral 1327, cantor 1333, provost 1339/1343.  Canon at Schwerin Cathedral 1328. 
2 CONT * 3.         '''JOHANN''' .  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ names "fratres Gherardus, Ghiselbertus et Iohannes domicellus, filii Hinrici comitis"[207]. 
2 CONT * 4.         '''ADELHEID''' [Agnes] (-[1349/50]).  The Chronicon Holtzatiæ refers to "filiam [Hinrici comitis]" as the wife of "duci Sleszwiccensi" and mother of "dux Woldemarus postea…rex Dacie"[208].  m firstly (1313) ERICH II H
2 CONC erzog von Schleswig, son of WALDEMAR IV Herzog von Schleswig & his first wife Elisabeth von Sachsen-Lauenburg (-12 Mar 1325, bur Schleswig Cathedral).  m secondly ([21 Sep 1326/22 Feb 1333]) DIETRICH Graf von Honstein in Heringen 
2 CONC und Hohenstein (-1379). 
2 CONT * 5.         '''ELISABETH''' ([1300]-before 1340).  Her parentage is confirmed by the Chronica Jutensis which records disputes between "Christoferum" and "comitem Gerardum", adding that "rex Ericus" repudiated "sororem eius"[209].
2 CONC   m firstly ([1315]) JOHANN II Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen & his wife Ingeborg of Sweden (-22 Apr 1322).  m secondly (1330, divorced 1331) ERIK of Denmark, son of CHRISTOF
2 CONC FER II King of Denmark & his wife Euphemia of Pomerania-Wolgast ([1307]-Kiel early 1332, bur Sorø Abbey). 
2 CONT * 6.         '''ERMENGARD''' (-27 Dec after 1329).  “Ermegard comitissa et Gerhardus ipsius filius comes in Hoya” exchanged property with Kloster Bücken by charter dated 9 Dec 1326[210].  m (Papal dispensation 4o Avignon 25 Jan 13
2 CONC 23) OTTO [I] Graf von Hoya zu Nienburg, son of HEINRICH [II] Graf von Hoya & his second wife Jutta von Ravensberg (-[23 Apr/2 Aug] 1324). 
2 CONT
